  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1220 PM CDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nTonight through next Friday...While some fluctuation in these \nfeatures will exist across the region, high pressure at both the \nsurface and aloft will overall continue to dominate the weather \nacross the forecast area through much of this forecast period. \nThis'll continue to result in quiet weather across the CWA through \nthe majority of the period.  Unfortunately, high temperatures will \ngradually warm a few degrees each day across the area, but through \nmid-week the drier airmass currently over the region will remain \npresent under easterly flow.  Despite the warming afternoon high \ntemperatures, this dry air will allow for pleasant overnight lows as \nthey generally range from the upper 50s to middle 60s through \nTuesday night.\n\nDuring the mid and latter portions of the week, moisture will subtly \nbegin increasing again across the region as southerly flow at the \nsurface and aloft returns.  In turn, rain chances will also begin \nincreasing each afternoon Wednesday through Friday as the \naforementioned high aloft steadily slides east of the Lower \nMississippi River Valley through week's end.  Increased troughing to \nthe west across the southern plains states could yield a cold front \nthat may try to shift east into the forecast area sometime next \nweekend.  This would allow rain chances to persist across the CWA \nduring that time. /19/",
